_override": 1, "_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn9le08ob03re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn9le08ob03re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn9le08ob03re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn9le08ob03re2img01.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "So you remember the story about Hansel, the young man who has been told to find a wife? He's been given three keys. He has been told to choose whatever he wants from the rooms they open. Now, he's standing in the castle.<br/><br/>The first room is open and the contents are being considered. The guard at the door told Hansel that he was the first person to unlock that room! He says that everything this room contained is covered in pearls. Hansel replied that he wouldn't be in there long. When Hansel comest out, the guard is shocked to find  the simplest single pearl necklace has been chosen."}, {"time": "39000", "image": "engenn9le08ob03re2img02.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "Now the second door is being opened. This door has been closed for decades. The guard asks Hansel if he knew it had been filled with silver objects before he was born.  Most of the silver, candlesticks and jewelry and chalices is being displayed on large oak tables around the room. Hansel chooses a plain silver cup.<br/><br/>When the third door is opened and a golden object has been picked out, Hansel goes back to the pond. A beautiful young woman is standing there."}, {"time": "72000", "image": "engenn9le08ob03re2img03.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "She smiles and tells Hansel that he has saved her. She continues saying that because he chose the simplest things, the castle was his. She tells him he could marry whoever he wanted.\nThen, the young woman changes into a beautiful white dove and flies away.<br/><br/>Hansel marries a simple woman, and they live happily ever after."}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Storytelling"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Hansel at the Castle"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 8}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "  Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le08ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Passive: The Present Continuous and Present Perfect Tenses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Present Continuous to talk about an action that is happening at the time of speaking. The action or event is in progress. <br/><span class=\"italic\">Few people actually know what exactly <span class=\"strong\">is happening</span> to the ozone layer.</span><br/><br/>You use the Present Perfect to talk about a finished action or event with present consequences. There is a connection between what happened in the past and the present.<br/><span class=\"italic\">Someone <span class=\"strong\">has given</span> him three keys.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You often choose the passive form when you want to talk about an action but are not so interested in saying who or what does/did it. Passives without <span class=\"italic\">agents</span> (the doers) are common in storytelling. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart below for the structure of the passive voice."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Name\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Present Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" am/are/is +  being + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> The first room is open and the contents <span class=\\\"strong\\\">are being considered</span>.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Present Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" have/has + been + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> He <span class=\\\"strong\\\">has been given</span> three keys.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "The first room is open and the contents are being considered."}, {"type": "example", "content": "So you remember the story about Hansel, the young man who has been told to find a wife? He has been given three keys. He has been told to choose whatever he wants from the rooms they open."}, {"type": "example", "content": "When Hansel comest out, the guard is shocked to find  the simplest single pearl necklace has been chosen."}, {"type": "example", "content": " Most of the silver, candlesticks and jewelry and chalices, is being displayed on large oak tables around the room. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "When the third door is opened and a golden object has been picked out, Hansel goes back to the pond. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Reported Speech and Questions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use reported speech (indirect speech) when you are saying (reporting) what other people said. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "This style of writing is common in storytelling. It allows the writer to share dialogue with the reader without always using quotation marks."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you tell people what someone has said you generally make the verb tense 'more in the past' since we are reporting the information at a later time. You need to change the verb to the next past form. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Direct speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Reported speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\u201cI <span class=\\\"strong\\\">hate</span> him.\u201d  \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He said he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">hated</span> him.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\u201cI<span class=\\\"strong\\\">'m coming</span> to the party.\u201d  \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He said he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">was coming</span>. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\u201cI already <span class=\\\"strong\\\">know</span>.\u201d  \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He said he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">had already</span> known.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\u201cI <span class=\\\"strong\\\">can</span> swim.\u201d\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She told me she <span class=\\\"strong\\\">could</span> swim.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You have to change the pronoun if you are reporting what someone else said. Compare these two sentences. In each case the person actually said \"I don't want to go.\""}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>I said, \u201cI don't want to go.\u201d  >  I said <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">I</span></span> didn't want to go.</li><li>Beth said, \u201cI don't want to go.\u201d  >  Beth said <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">she</span></span> didn't want to go.</li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you want to report questions asked, the subject normally comes before the verb."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"underline\">Direct</span>:<span class=\"italic\"> Hansel replied \u201cI won't be in there long.\u201d</span><br/><span class=\"underline\">Indirect</span>:<span class=\"italic\"> Hansel replied that <span class=\"strong\">he wouldn't be in there long</span>.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When the question is a yes/no question, you use <span class=\"italic\">if</span> or <span class=\"italic\">whether</span> to report it."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">The guard asks Hansel <span class=\"strong\">if/whether</span> he knew it has been filled with silver objects before he was born.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart below to see the changes in verb tense."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":10,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Direct speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Reported speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Simple Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Simple Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Simple Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Present Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past Perfect Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Future Simple (will)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Conditional (would)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal Can\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal Could\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal May\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal Might\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal Will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal Would\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "The guard at the door told Hansel that he was the first person to unlock that room!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "He says that everything this room contained was covered in pearls. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Hansel replied that he wouldn't be in there long."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The guard informs Hansel it was filled with silver objects before he was born."}, {"type": "example", "content": "She smiles and tells Hansel that he has saved her. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "She continues saying that because he chose the simplest things, the castle was his. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "She tells him he could marry whoever he wanted."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The guard asks  Hansel if he knew it has been filled with silver objects before he was born. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "castle "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a \u200blarge \u200bbuilding, \u200bbuilt in the past by a \u200bruler to \u200bprotect the \u200bpeople inside from the outside"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Now, he's standing in the castle. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le08ob03aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you hear in a fairytale."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to unlock"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to \u200bopen something, \u200bespecially a \u200bdoor that is \u200blocked "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The guard at the door told Hansel that he was the first person to unlock that room!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le08ob03aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pearl "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a \u200bsmall, round \u200bobject that \u200bforms around a \u200bgrain of \u200bsand inside the \u200bshell of a \u200bsea \u200bcreature"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Everything this room contained was covered in pearls. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le08ob03aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "decade "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a \u200bperiod of ten \u200byears"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This door has been closed for decades."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le08ob03aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "guard"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a \u200bperson whose \u200bjob is to \u200bprotect a \u200bplace or someone from \u200bdanger or \u200battack"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The guard at the door told Hansel that he was the first person to unlock that room! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le08ob03aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "candlestick "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an \u200bobject that \u200bholds a \u200bcandle"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Most of the silver, candlesticks and jewelry and chalices are being displayed on large oak tables."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le08ob03aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "chalice "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a large cup, used for drinking wine"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The chalice is being displayed on a large oak table. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le08ob03aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dove "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a \u200bwhite or \u200bgrey \u200bbird, often used as a \u200bsymbol of \u20